# s1_weight_stream: thirteen SPU dispatches, each layer's weights shared just in time.
#
# impl_snapshot: snni_bert_puma_stream.py
# Whole driver, selected by PUMA_DRIVER below.
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: pybind11::bytes
# cost_class: free
#
# choice     rank 1 at the baseline's peak:
#              5,528.6 MB  75.6%  pybind11::bytes <- PyBytes_FromStringAndSize      <- this step
#              1,125.2 MB  15.0%  python3.10+0x28728a <- _PyBytes_Resize
#                437.7 MB   5.8%  python3.10+0x2c7866 <- PyBytes_FromStringAndSize
# arm rule   closed arm (borrowed levers only). Donor: SHAFT-CPU x0_per_layer_base .. x4_stream_load
#            (17.08.), transcript-identical to the whole-model program (11,228,688,384 B, 1495 rounds),
#            gate byte-identical.
# order      line reordered 17.08.: s1_response_stream_v2 had skipped rank 1 (frame above inside the
#            libspu.so wheel); the arena is filled by what the driver asks SPU to hold, so a driver
#            change reaches it. response_stream_v2 on top of this step: +1.9%, n=3
#            (off-path-runs/s2_response_stream_on_ws/); its -12.4% at baseline is kept as evidence.
# census     off-path-runs/p_census/: 5.36 GB = parameter-share serialization arena; halving the
#            layers moved the peak 2,188,504 kB (2.04 GB predicted, within 7%).
# refuted    s1_layer_infeed: staging the transfer alone does nothing (one SPU computation holds all
#            parameters). Retired campaign: 05_perlayer no-op (XLA liveness), 06_stream -57%.
# lever      13 dispatches (embeddings, 12 layers, head); each layer's parameters shared right before
#            its dispatch, then `del` + gc.collect(). layer_fn shape-identical: compiled once.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# measured
#   s1_response_stream_v2   6,406,676 kB
#   s2_weight_stream        3,005,148 / 3,042,832 / 2,992,064, median 3,005,148   -53.1%
#   wall                          298 / 298 / 300 s
# cost       declared paid before the run (twelve sharing rounds instead of one); measured free:
#              s1_response_stream_v2   wall 365 s
#              s2_weight_stream        wall 298 s   -10.6%, against a 0.778% wall spread
#            (one compile of the layer body, smaller working set). No transcript counters on PUMA
#            (comm_bytes NA); traffic declared from the mechanism.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gate       passes (not a phase B row):
#              s1  logits 0.3707122802734375  -0.03607940673828125   absmax 8.2497482299804688
#              s2  logits 0.37026214599609375 -0.036106109619140625  absmax 8.2437324523925781
#            max movement 6.0e-3 absolute; gate_tolerance_abs 1.4e-2 (MANIFEST.md).
# equiv      in every run: EQUIV|stream_vs_whole|max_abs=0|max_rel=0 (run1..run3). The driver runs the
#            streamed and whole-model paths in plaintext and exits 7 on any difference.
PUMA_DRIVER=snni_bert_puma_stream.py
